I am sitting at my desk in the office.
I arrived early today.
I have already worked here for half a year.
Suddenly Peter and Eva come over to my desk.
Peter is carrying a small cake with a single candle.
"Happy birthday, Maya!" they say in unison.
I become really happy and very surprised.
"Thank you very much," I say to them.
"I have never celebrated my birthday in Denmark before."
Eva smiles broadly.
"We bought the cake at the bakery this morning," she explains.
"Yes, and I have made coffee for us," Peter adds.
He places a large cup of coffee on my table.
"You are simply so sweet," I say.
"I do not feel thirty-two years old at all."
"When I worked in Mexico, we rarely got cake in the morning."
Peter and Eva pull two chairs over to the desk.
We eat the cake together, and it is a fantastic start to my day.
